        <localActions>
            <fullName>compare_headroom_179We000000qAMj</fullName>
            <description>Concise multi-country Headroom comparison. Resolves ONE governed program/category across SEVERAL countries for a fiscal year and returns a single compact comparison — a lead interpretation, one compact line per country (Funding Gap or Available Headroom, with Secured and Pipeline), and which country has the largest gap — instead of a full financial block per country. Each country is resolved through the same governed engine as a single-country query, so the figures match. Use this whenever the user asks for headroom or funding gap for one program across two or more countries.</description>
            <developerName>compare_headroom_179We000000qAMj</developerName>
            <invocationTarget>AmaizeCompareHeadroom</invocationTarget>
            <invocationTargetType>apex</invocationTargetType>
            <isConfirmationRequired>false</isConfirmationRequired>
            <isIncludeInProgressIndicator>false</isIncludeInProgressIndicator>
            <localDeveloperName>compare_headroom</localDeveloperName>
            <masterLabel>Compare Headroom</masterLabel>
        </localActions>
        <localActions>
            <fullName>analyze_headroom_179We000000qAMj</fullName>
            <description>Headroom aggregation for a single country. Supports PROGRAM MODE (a standard Headroom category — Core Program, Rural Retail, Market Access, Trees, System Change Extension, Unrestricted, Working Capital) and DIMENSION MODE (an explicit lower-level Budget Line dimension value the user named — a Cost Category, Department, Cost Type, or Sub-Unit such as Crop Insurance, Staff Costs, Field Operations). Providing BOTH a program and a dimension value segments the program (Program + Dimension). It SUMS the same stored fields across every qualifying line for the country and fiscal year. Returns &apos;summary&apos; (concise conversational answer, the default) and &apos;detail&apos; (full breakdown, on request). found=true with a result; or found=false with signal AMBIGUOUS (the value exists in more than one dimension — the summary asks which), NOT_FOUND (the value is in no dimension for that scope), NONE, NOT_CONFIGURED, Not Applicable, or NEEDS_INFO.</description>
            <developerName>analyze_headroom_179We000000qAMj</developerName>
            <invocationTarget>AmaizeAnalyzeHeadroom</invocationTarget>
            <invocationTargetType>apex</invocationTargetType>
            <isConfirmationRequired>false</isConfirmationRequired>
            <isIncludeInProgressIndicator>false</isIncludeInProgressIndicator>
            <localDeveloperName>analyze_headroom</localDeveloperName>
            <masterLabel>Analyze Headroom</masterLabel>
        </localActions>
